<CONTENT>In Section 3, “Information Required From All Proposal Submitters,” under subsection A, “Minimum Consultant Requirements,” the RFP states:

1. “The firm must have at least $2 Billion under management.”

So, the minimum amount of assets under management required is $2 billion.

Relevant context from the same minimum requirements section:
- The firm must work with public pension funds.
- The lead consultant assigned to the account must have at least 10 years of investment experience.
- The firm must agree to serve as a fiduciary to APFRS under Alaska and other applicable law.
- The firm must be registered as an Investment Advisor under the Investment Advisers Act of 1940.

Note that this $2 billion requirement applies to the investment consultant firm, not to individual client accounts.</CONTENT>
