<CONTENT>The retirement system is the Texas Municipal Retirement System (TMRS).

Relevant evidence:
- The document is titled “Request for Proposal (RFP) – Non-Discretionary General Investment Consulting Services.”
- In Section IV, “General Information & Minimum Requirements,” TMRS states that it is seeking proposals from qualified general investment consultants currently providing general investment consulting advice on a non-discretionary basis to public pension plans larger than $5 billion.
- Under Section IV(I), “Minimum Eligibility Requirements,” item 1 specifically requires:
  “Respondent must be currently providing general investment advice on a non-discretionary basis to at least 5 public pension plans larger than $5 billion and at least 2 public plans over $20 billion.”

Therefore, the answer is TMRS, the Texas Municipal Retirement System.</CONTENT>
