<CONTENT>The due diligence questionnaire is the one labeled:

“APPENDIX A – DUE DILIGENCE QUESTIONNAIRE”

Within that questionnaire, the relevant prompt appears under:

“4.0 Proposed Fund Investment Strategy”

More precisely, it is question 4.6, which states:

“Describe respondent’s proposal for how the Fund will invest the capital in NJ-based, Life Science/ Healthcare companies. What percentage of respondent’s current portfolio companies are located in NJ? What percentage of current portfolio companies are Life Science/ Healthcare companies?”

This identifies the questionnaire as a New Jersey-focused due diligence questionnaire tied to a proposed fund strategy centered on NJ-based Life Science/Healthcare companies.

Relevant contextual clues from the same questionnaire:
- It asks about management team involvement in community or business organizations active in New Jersey.
- It asks about SSBCI personnel or professional connections.
- It focuses on investing capital in New Jersey-based Life Science/Healthcare companies.
- It also asks about organizations that help facilitate a pipeline of New Jersey Life Science/Healthcare startups seeking seed or start-up capital.

So, the answer is: the question is asked in the “Appendix A – Due Diligence Questionnaire,” specifically section 4.6 of the proposed fund investment strategy section.</CONTENT>
