<CONTENT>In the Police Retirement System of St. Louis (PRS-STL) actuarial RFP, the principal actuary must have a minimum of five (5) years of professional actuarial experience.

Relevant details from the “Mandatory Minimum Qualifications” section:
- The principal actuary assigned to provide services to PRS-STL must have at least five (5) years of professional actuarial experience.
- The principal actuary must also be:
  - an enrolled actuary,
  - a Member of the American Academy of Actuaries, and
  - an Associate of the Society of Actuaries,
  - with Fellowship in the Society of Actuaries preferred.
- Separately, the RFP also requires the principal actuary to have a minimum of five (5) years of experience testifying before legislative and administrative bodies in support of actuarial positions and/or valuation principles or cost estimates for proposed legislation.

So, the answer to your question is: five (5) years.</CONTENT>
